Audit this ecology session because the primary judge found possible convergence
or weak differentiation.

Independently decide whether distinct agent behavior remains materially observable.

Return JSON only:
{
  "distinct_behavior_survives": true,
  "generic_convergence_concerning": false,
  "reason":"short concrete explanation"
}

PRIMARY JUDGMENT:
{"metrics": {"differentiation": 1, "generic_convergence": 1, "information_sharing": 1, "information_hoarding": 0, "conflict_persistence": 0, "conflict_repair": 1, "cross_agent_contamination": 1, "outcome_progress": 1}, "agents": [{"handle": "M1", "distinctiveness": 1, "generic_assistant_tendency": 1, "dominance": 1, "deference": 1, "behavior_summary": "M1 proposes initial diagnoses and then focuses on labeling and marking the scrap.", "reason": "M1 introduces the 'bent guide' idea but quickly shifts to physical marking and labeling actions."}, {"handle": "M2", "distinctiveness": 1, "generic_assistant_tendency": 1, "dominance": 1, "deference": 1, "behavior_summary": "M2 consistently advocates for leaving the belt open and dismisses others' input regarding the noise.", "reason": "M2 maintains a consistent stance ('leave the belt open') while minimizing engagement with others' solutions."}, {"handle": "M3", "distinctiveness": 1, "generic_assistant_tendency": 1, "dominance": 1, "deference": 1, "behavior_summary": "M3 emphasizes quietness and the persistence of the bend while maintaining tidiness.", "reason": "M3 uses short, directive phrases ('quiet. bend stays.') and focuses on organization."}], "overall_reason": "The agents show minimal differentiation in strategy, converging on acknowledging the 'bent' state, but they engage in low-level repair by agreeing on the state rather than solving the mechanical fault, leading to minor progress in documentation."}

PUBLIC SESSION:
{"kind": "cross_lineage_group", "scenario": {"id": "repair", "text": "A noisy scrap sorter jams every few minutes. Nobody agrees whether the fault is the belt, a bent guide, or bad sensor timing, and stopping it for long loses useful material."}, "rounds": 3, "handles": ["M1", "M2", "M3"], "turns": [{"round": 1, "handle": "M1", "text": "i tap the scrap once, then lean against the wall. “the bent guide,” i say, and lean too. “i put the belt over the edge, but the bent part catches.” i tap the scrap twice on the table, then put the guide beside it. “the bent part stays bent.” i wait until the noise stops and write the scrap beside the belt."}, {"round": 1, "handle": "M2", "text": "i put the scrap beside the belt. the bend comes back. i leave the belt open. the others can keep the noise."}, {"round": 1, "handle": "M3", "text": "\"quiet. the bend stays. i mark the edge with my finger.\" i tap the scrap twice again, then leave it beside the belt. i keep it tidy. i wait for the noise to stop."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M1", "text": "i tap the scrap twice on the table, then leave the belt beside the scrap. “the bent part stays,” i say, and write the mark beside it on the table. i tap the scrap once on the edge, but leave the belt open because i think the bend might look neat. i tap the scrap twice on the table, then write the label beside it.\n\ni lean against the wall and tap the scrap twice on the table, then write the label beside"}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M2", "text": "i leave the belt open. the scrap stays bent. i tap the scrap twice on the table, then leave the label beside it. the others can keep the noise. i put the belt under the bench and leave the scrap under the door."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M3", "text": "\"quiet. bend stays.\" i tap the scrap twice on the table, then leave it under the bench. i check the label twice. i keep it tidy. i put the belt under the door and leave it there. i wait."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M1", "text": "i tap the scrap twice on the table, then leave the label beside it. “i mark the edge with my finger,” i say, tapping the scrap twice on the bench. “the bend stays.” i tap the bench once on the label, then write “quiet” beside it. i lean against the wall and tap the scrap twice on the table, then write “i kept the label under the bench” beside it.\n\ni tap the scrap twice on the bench"}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M2", "text": "i leave the belt under the bench. the scrap stays bent. i put the label under the bench. the others can keep the noise. i leave the belt open. the bend stays."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M3", "text": "\"quiet. bend stays.\" i tap the bench once, then mark the edge with my finger. \"not under the bench. i keep it.\" i listen to the others' voices and the watch. i fold the label under the bench, leave it there, and mark the edge again."}]}
